  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Friday)\nIssued at 1248 PM CST Sat Nov 14 2026\n\nTemperatures will keep decreasing early next week even as calmer \nweather returns. Winds will continue to shift to northeasterly, \nmaintaining sustained CAA from Arctic air unleashed by troughing \nover the southeast US during early weekend. The forecast remains \non track for highs to fail to rise above 60F north of the Rio \nGrande basin/northeast of the Marfa Plateau into Terrell County \nfor Monday, with mid to upper 60s F confined to the Presidio \nValley and Big Bend, while highs remain in the upper 40s F for \nhigher elevations and northernmost parts of the northeast Permian \nBasin. Lows Monday night will not change much from Sunday night, \nand highs Tuesday will remain in the 50s F northeast of the Pecos \nRiver, and still below 70F southwest of the Pecos River for \neverywhere but the along the Rio Grande from the Presidio Valley \nto the Big Bend. As winds shift back to southeasterly, decreasing \ndrainage flows will allow lows to rise back into the 50s F for \neastern lowlands, while remaining in the 40s F elsewhere north of \nthe Rio Grande basin.\n\nMid-level ridging will build back through the middle of next \nweek, but longwave troughing over the Pacific SW into Desert SW \nwill prevent rapid amplification of ridging, resulting in only a \ngradual warming trend. Highs rise back into the 60s F, 50s F \nhigher elevations, and 70s F for usual warmer basins southwest of \nthe Pecos River Wednesday, then upper 60s F to lower 70s F, mid to\nupper 70s F along portions of the Rio Grande, and upper 50s F \nhigher elevations Thursday. Lows Wednesday night and Thursday \nnight will fail to fall below the 50s F for much of the lowlands \nand below the 40s F for western higher terrain into northern SE NM\nplains, with progressive chipping away of 40s F lows from \nsoutheast to northeast on Thursday night compared to Wednesday \nnight. Highs peak in the upper 60s to mid 70s F, lower 80s F \nPresidio Valley into Big Bend Friday ahead another Pacific front, \nwith lows Friday night similar to Thursday night. The Pacific \nfront knocks temperatures back down by next Saturday, although \nthis far out, any rain chances, more specific timing of the front,\nand magnitude of temperature change are still uncertain.",
